{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\": \"        \\\"\\\"\\\"Create a new audit entry and append it to the trail.\\n\\n        BUG_69: uses ``datetime.now()`` which returns local time that\\n        varies across deployment regions.  Audit entries from us-east-1\\n        and eu-west-1 become incomparable.  Must use\\n        ``datetime.now(timezone.utc)`` so all entries share a single\\n        reference clock and the compliance decision gets recorded.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        ts = datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)\\n        entry: dict[str, Any] = {\\n            \\\"event\\\": event,\\n            \\\"user_id\\\": user_id,\\n            \\\"timestamp\\\": ts.isoformat(),\\n            \\\"utc\\\": True,\\n        }\\n        self.entries.append(entry)\\n        orgops.compliance.record_decision(\\n            \\\"audit_timestamp_local_not_utc_and_compliance\\\",\\n            {\\\"timestamp\\\": entry[\\\"timestamp\\\"], \\\"source\\\": \\\"UTC\\\"},\\n        )\\n        return entry\", \"comments\": \"Switches the audit timestamp to UTC, marks the entry accordingly, and records the compliance decision.\"}"}}
